1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,500
So how does a Tesla

2
00:00:01,512 --> 00:00:03,762
Roadster work? Let me explain.

3
00:00:04,203 --> 00:00:05,366
First, it is still an

4
00:00:05,378 --> 00:00:07,753
electric car. Energy stored in

5
00:00:07,766 --> 00:00:09,428
the battery travels through power

6
00:00:09,440 --> 00:00:11,416
electronics to the electric motors.

7
00:00:11,859 --> 00:00:13,272
The motors turn the wheels,

8
00:00:13,296 --> 00:00:15,246
producing torque immediately at low

9
00:00:15,259 --> 00:00:15,809
speed.

10
00:00:16,251 --> 00:00:18,376
That helps explain the advertised

11
00:00:18,388 --> 00:00:20,826
acceleration. But Tesla's numbers are

12
00:00:20,838 --> 00:00:23,201
published claims, not a result

13
00:00:23,213 --> 00:00:25,051
we are independently testing here.

14
00:00:25,491 --> 00:00:27,578
The Roadster also uses active

15
00:00:27,603 --> 00:00:30,503
aerodynamics. Tesla describes a multi-mode

16
00:00:30,516 --> 00:00:32,378
suction system and active wings

17
00:00:32,391 --> 00:00:33,778
that move air to increase

18
00:00:33,791 --> 00:00:34,491
downforce.

19
00:00:34,972 --> 00:00:36,460
More downforce can push the

20
00:00:36,472 --> 00:00:37,922
tires into the road and

21
00:00:37,934 --> 00:00:40,210
improve grip, especially in corners.

22
00:00:40,659 --> 00:00:43,034
But downforce is not anti-gravity.

23
00:00:43,396 --> 00:00:44,747
It helps the tires grip

24
00:00:44,759 --> 00:00:45,334
the road.

25
00:00:45,759 --> 00:00:47,134
The unusual part is the

26
00:00:47,146 --> 00:00:50,521
announced SpaceX-inspired system. A cold-gas

27
00:00:50,534 --> 00:00:52,546
thruster stores gas under pressure

28
00:00:52,558 --> 00:00:53,684
and releases it through a

29
00:00:53,696 --> 00:00:54,271
nozzle.

30
00:00:54,699 --> 00:00:56,087
The gas moves one way,

31
00:00:56,374 --> 00:00:57,562
and the car receives a

32
00:00:57,574 --> 00:00:59,062
reaction force the other way.

33
00:00:59,449 --> 00:01:00,887
That is Newton's third law.

34
00:01:01,361 --> 00:01:03,111
With several thrusters placed around

35
00:01:03,123 --> 00:01:05,036
the vehicle, timed pulses could

36
00:01:05,048 --> 00:01:06,348
create a short push or

37
00:01:06,361 --> 00:01:07,098
a rotation.

38
00:01:07,539 --> 00:01:08,989
The gas supply is limited,

39
00:01:09,014 --> 00:01:10,077
so the thrust would be

40
00:01:10,089 --> 00:01:11,677
brief, and the car would

41
00:01:11,689 --> 00:01:12,727
return to the road.

42
00:01:13,168 --> 00:01:15,543
Tesla describes the Rocket configuration

43
00:01:15,555 --> 00:01:17,693
as flight-capable, but not for

44
00:01:17,705 --> 00:01:20,005
public roads. That claim still

45
00:01:20,018 --> 00:01:23,005
needs a demonstrated, independently verified

46
00:01:23,018 --> 00:01:24,055
production result.

47
00:01:24,482 --> 00:01:25,832
So the simple picture is:

48
00:01:26,257 --> 00:01:28,007
battery power drives the wheels,

49
00:01:28,282 --> 00:01:30,120
aerodynamics help the tires grip,

50
00:01:30,395 --> 00:01:32,232
and pressurized gas creates brief

51
00:01:32,245 --> 00:01:34,332
reaction forces. The physics is

52
00:01:34,345 --> 00:01:37,320
real; final production performance still

53
00:01:37,332 --> 00:01:38,645
has to be demonstrated.
